infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title The exchange inversion: why funnel, not distribute
  desc Fairness forces one total order — the opposite of the unit's distribute-for-scale playbook
  compares
    - label Distribute for scale
      children
        - label Parallel threads on shared state
          desc The unit's instinct: spread work for throughput
        - label Order decided by lock scheduling
          desc Relative order is nondeterministic
        - label Replicas can disagree on who filled first
          desc No single total order to audit
        - label Scale by adding threads
          desc Concurrency is the lever
    - label Funnel through one sequencer
      children
        - label Single-threaded matching core
          desc One total order, applied event-by-event
        - label Order fixed by global sequence number
          desc Deterministic: same inputs, same trades
        - label Every replica and replay agrees
          desc Recovery and audit are exact
        - label Scale the one thread, partition by instrument
          desc Faster thread (no locks, book in cache)
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
